mastery.solution_text:
Each interval is $0.002$. Thus $2.786$ is three intervals after $2.780$; $2.781$ and $2.789$ lie halfway within their intervals.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(5.5,0);
\foreach \x in {0,...,5} {\draw (\x,0.12)--(\x,-0.12);}
\node[below] at (0,-0.12) {$2.780$};
\node[below] at (5,-0.12) {$2.790$};
\fill (0.5,0) circle (2.2pt); \node[above] at (0.5,0.15) {$2.781$};
\fill (3,0) circle (2.2pt); \node[above] at (3,0.15) {$2.786$};
\fill (4.5,0) circle (2.2pt); \node[above] at (4.5,0.15) {$2.789$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

